{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/658144-lashing-out-against-effects-and-results","id":658144,"title":"Lashing Out Against Effects and Results","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-09T10:59:25-07:00","id":658144,"title":"Lashing Out Against Effects and Results","content":"So for things like Awe, it says that a vampire can defend by Lashing Out. If they succeed, then they aren't affected. Does this form of Lashing Out not generate the same results, or would &quot;Flight&quot; in this case mean that the effect stops working? Does the vampire being Lashed Out at still receive the relevant Condition for being Lashed Out against? What would happen if a vampire using Awe decides to Fight the Kindred who Lashed Out against them?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T11:22:18-07:00","id":658180,"title":"","content":"Betty uses Awe<br /> <br /> Ron spends the willpower and lashes out with Monsterious beast<br /> <br /> Betty Feels Ron's Beast imposing on her. She lashes out with her Seductive Beast. (Option b she leaves the scene)<br /> <br /> Clash of Wills (i believe)<br /> <br /> Loser takes the condition<br /> <br /> i.e: Ron takes wanton if Betty wins<br /> <br /> i.e2: Betty takes Shaken(i think?) if Ron wins<br /> <br /> In case of tie both kindred take the conditions relevant to the unchained beast.<br /> <br /> ----------------------------<br /> <br /> I believe that's how it plays out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","user":"Mal","date":".  some grammar and spelling 09-09-2015, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T11:34:37-07:00","id":658187,"title":"","content":"<br /> The language around Lashing Out just made me feel like it prompts a Frenzy-esque state, wherein the target <i>literally</i> either Fights or Flees. Is this just evocative imagery, and in the case of Betty vs Ron, if Ron Lashes Out and wins, then Betty is still there, still using Awe against anybody else in the scene, but is suffering from the Condition and Ron gets a +2 against her?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/658144-lashing-out-against-effects-and-results?p=658180#post658180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i.e2: Betty takes Shaken(i think?) if Ron wins</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bestial Condition actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T11:43:38-07:00","id":658190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/658144-lashing-out-against-effects-and-results?p=658187#post658187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The language around Lashing Out just made me feel like it prompts a Frenzy-esque state, wherein the target <i>literally</i> either Fights or Flees. Is this just evocative imagery, and in the case of Betty vs Ron, if Ron Lashes Out and wins, then Betty is still there, still using Awe against anybody else in the scene, but is suffering from the Condition and Ron gets a +2 against her?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just evocative imagery. To &quot;fight&quot; in a Predatory Aura contest doesn't literally mean to come to blows, and to &quot;flee&quot; doesn't literally mean to run away. It's just contesting the challenge or backing down from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T19:41:53-07:00","id":658824,"title":"","content":"I read and interrupted it the same as BigDamnHero if you don't fight in the contest than you take the condition. IT says if you Flee you avoid getting the condition. Since Aura is AoE the only way to Flee is to leave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T20:11:46-07:00","id":658851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/658144-lashing-out-against-effects-and-results?p=658824#post658824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read and interrupted it the same as BigDamnHero if you don't fight in the contest than you take the condition. IT says if you Flee you avoid getting the condition. Since Aura is AoE the only way to Flee is to leave.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you still gain the Condition if you Flee.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Flight:</b> This represents a stark withdrawal. It costs nothing, and allows for a reasonable out from the challenge. This usually means a convenient escape or excuse to pull away. It typically makes the character look inferior or foolish. The aggressor may pursue. The victim gains the Condition associated with the initiating vampire\u2019s aspect of the Beast. </div> </div> </div>Also, to me that description doesn't say you have to run away, it says you back down or weasel out of the challenge, usually in a way that makes you look bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-09-2015, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T20:33:22-07:00","id":658858,"title":"","content":"For instance if you turned on Awe and someone lashed out and you turned off Awe, that would count as flight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}